nce; advanced exports remain available to scripts.\n:icons query=<name> discovers installed canonical Lucide names (paged); create icons / apply op=lucide insert editable native groups. groupMap maps logical icon aliases to groupId/elementIds; idMap remains single-element only. Defaults: size=96, strokeColor=#1e1e1e, roughness=1, opacity=100; optional strokeWidth is final scene units. No trusted script is required.\n:script requires trusted=true and an explicit existing local script file. utils.input contains args; utils.excalidrawLib is the installed runtime. Await all work; completion does not imply saved drawing.\nOne-shot EA is cleaned up; utility prompts fail INTERACTION_REQUIRED. Trusted code can still invoke other interactive APIs: this is not a sandbox, timeout cancellation or transaction.\nExport names an explicit out=.svg/.png; overwrite=true is required for existing outputs. Live exports never implicitly save. Disk exports require local Vault assets; use a loaded live source or placeholders for remote assets.\nFor cheap previews: :read detail=images, then :export imagePolicy={"default":"placeholder","rules":[{"ids":["wanted-id"],"mode":"original"}]}. This is lossless for the underlying drawing, not the preview.\nimageMetadata apply operations set bounded descriptive label/tags, with null clearing; request-only imagePolicy.labels does not persist. Thumbnail mode uses thumbnailMaxDimension=512 by default; only PNG/JPEG/WebP with safe preflight dimensions are decoded (24 MiB / 16 million pixels maximum).\nmaxWidth/maxHeight/maxPixels bound output dimensions; maxArtifactBytes caps final bytes. Source revision covers originals; representationId identifies the preview. SVG width controls display size, not embedded raster payload size; use imagePolicy for that.\nUse :schema for exact fields, operation limits, and runnable examples. Do not edit compressed drawing Markdown directly or install another Excalidraw CLI.\n',nC=2097152,aC=524288;class rC extends Error{c